I. Concerning the Applicable Tax Categories for Foreign-Invested Enterprises and Foreign Enterprises
In accordance with the provisions of the Decision, foreign-invested enterprises and foreign enterprises, in addition to applying the Interim Regulations of the People's Republic of China on Value-Added Tax, the Interim Regulations of the People's Republic of China on Consumption Tax, the Interim Regulations of the People's Republic of China on Business Tax, and the Income Tax Law of the People's Republic of China for Enterprises with Foreign Investment and Foreign Enterprises, shall also apply the following interim regulations:
(1) the Interim Regulations of the People's Republic of China on Land Appreciation Tax promulgated by the State Council on December 12, 1993;
(2) the Interim Regulations of the People's Republic of China on Resource Tax promulgated by the State Council on December 25, 1993;
(3) the Interim Regulations of the People's Republic of China on Stamp Tax promulgated by the State Council on August 6, 1988;
(4) the Interim Regulations on the Slaughter Tax promulgated by the Government Administration Council of the Central People's Government on December 19, 1950;
(5) the Interim Regulations on the Urban Real Estate Tax promulgated by the Government Administration Council of the Central People's Government on August 8, 1951;
(6) the Interim Regulations on the License Tax for Vehicles and Vessels promulgated by the Government Administration Council of the Central People's Government on September 13, 1951;
(7) the Interim Regulations on Deed Tax promulgated by the Government Administration Council of the Central People's Government on April 3, 1950.
In the course of tax reform, the State Council shall continue to revise and formulate new interim tax regulations, and foreign-invested enterprises and foreign enterprises shall accordingly enforce them in accordance with the provisions of the relevant regulations.
